{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>You shall no longer.</b> An imperative, like <i>lo tosifu</i> (you shall not add) (Deuteronomy 4:2)." "<b>Bring.</b> Like <i>lehavi</i> (to bring), for your grain-offering is vanity in My eyes, and the incense is an abomination." "<b>New moon.</b> Explained in the Torah (Numbers 28:14) that it is the head of the month." "<b>Call a calling.</b> That you call them <i>mikra'ei kodesh</i> (sacred convocations) (Leviticus 23:2), and He mentioned them alongside the burnt-offerings and the grain-offering because of the additional offerings." "<b>I cannot bear iniquity.</b> The word is missing a predicate, like <i>chamor lechem</i> (Exodus 1:16:20)." "And the meaning of <b>and assembly</b> is like <i>me'otzer</i> (restrained) and <i>mumashpat</i> (taken from justice) (Isaiah 53:8) — that you shall not do any work. The meaning: I cannot bear iniquity together with assembly, for what benefit is there in assembly together with iniquity?"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {4 "Ibn Ezra cites two verse references conflated; Exodus 1:16 does not contain this phrase. The citation may be corrupt or may refer to a different passage.", 5 "Reading הטע׳ as an abbreviation for הטעם (the meaning); the apostrophe-like mark suggests a truncated word."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:11.704512002Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}